{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428255-it-s-a-sailor-s-life-for-me","id":1428255,"title":"It's a sailor's life for me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-13T04:41:45-08:00","id":1428255,"title":"It's a sailor's life for me","content":"I've seen historical dramas about sailors where they obviously shout out orders about running a ship, and I've gone looking for breakdowns of how exactly wood &amp; canvas ships worked. The former doesn't really teach you anything at all, and for the latter I only seem to turn up results that are way too in-depth.<br /> <br /> Has anyone got a nice, light guide that teaches you just enough to facilitate sounding real cool when you try for sail stunts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T06:07:19-08:00","id":1428261,"title":"","content":"Postion 36!<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, what actually works in real life doesn't <i>sound good </i>in a piece of fiction (like Role Play). You'd be better off watching stuff like Pirates of the Carribean and the historical dramas that inspired you in the first place and copying what they say.<br /> <br /> <i>Unless </i>you game with someone who actually knows what they are talking about, then learning from them would be the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T06:40:32-08:00","id":1428263,"title":"","content":"Exalted 1e's Savage Seas supplement is actually pretty decent as a balance between actual nautical information and details that might matter to the game (like making you sound like you know your stuff for Stunts).<br /> <br /> It has things like a break down of what the different positions on a boat are commonly called in Creation, so if you're commanding a ship in combat you can work in the right officers to call orders to for what maneuvers your doing. There's a section on navigation in Creation so you can actually know how compasses work when magnets don't point north (they point to the Elemental Pole of Earth in the center).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T07:57:00-08:00","id":1428272,"title":"","content":"But the North Star does point North. So... there's that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-13T08:23:25-08:00","id":1428277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428255-it-s-a-sailor-s-life-for-me?p=1428272#post1428272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the North Star does point North. So... there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> but the fist of the north star just punches you - that's less useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As for RP on a ship?<br /> <br /> You need three things at the very least:<br /> 1) leadership<br /> someone who actually makes the choices, the captain. good all-round social stats help here, perhaps also dots in war if you want to command a crew during a fight.<br /> <br /> 2) navigation<br /> some good dots in sail, int and per help here, probably also lore and survival for reading the sea and maps<br /> <br /> 3) provisions<br /> If you're at sea for weeks/months, you will need food - also supplies to patch up your ship if there's a storm/battle damage. Some good gods in Bur help here. someone with dots in craft wood for ship maintenance also helps here, but that can be done via the crew if they're skilled enough (if you have a crew at all)<br /> <br /> <br /> As for getting around at sea: int-lore for map reading and per-sail for matching the desired heading.f you can simplify it to a single int-sail roll if you want to keep it really simple.<br /> <br /> Fishing along the way can be per-sur, to spot where it'll be worthwhile to toss a net, or int-sur if you're nets based on conventional wisdom of where its good to set nets (but that wont work if you're on the move)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T09:59:43-08:00","id":1428363,"title":"","content":"The film Master &amp; Commander is both an excellent film and apparently crazy historically accurate, at least as far as the sailing and things go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T21:30:56-08:00","id":1428556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1428255-it-s-a-sailor-s-life-for-me?p=1428263#post1428263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted 1e's Savage Seas supplement is actually pretty decent as a balance between actual nautical information and details that might matter to the game (like making you sound like you know your stuff for Stunts)</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious, I didn't even know that existed. I came in early in 2e. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I'll try watching tv too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T02:52:29-08:00","id":1428723,"title":"","content":"Some basic details.<br /> <br /> You hoist sails<br /> <br /> Tacking into the wind is a way of sailing when you don't have the wind behind you<br /> <br /> Yard arms are the horizontal bits of a mast<br /> <br /> Port is left, starboard is right<br /> <br /> That covers like 90% of Hollywood nautical language.<br /> <br /> You can't go wrong with occassionally bellowing<br /> &quot;Hoist the main sail&quot; - unfurl the sails to get up to speed<br /> &quot;Hard to starboard&quot; - Turn hard to the right<br /> <br /> If you can find a good technical diagram of an older sailing ship (or even a fairly new sailing ship) you'll find a simply dizzying array of terms for various parts but few are dramatically appropriate.<br /> <br /> I would heartly second the recommendation for Master and Commander. But also any cheesy pirate film has all the classic nautical banter that might actually make sense.<br /> <br /> Of course it could be enjoyable to use nautical banter that doesn't make sense. &quot;Swab the mizzenmast!&quot;, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T06:51:12-08:00","id":1428746,"title":"","content":"Nothing wrong with \u201cBrace up yards ye crack-handed deck apes! Dying is the day worth livin\u2019 for!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T07:56:29-08:00","id":1428754,"title":"","content":"Might not be what you're looking for, but some links that I've found useful for players below:<br /> <br /> 1. Handy explanation for wind/direction and points of sail:<a href=\"https://www.hobie.com/articles/basics-sailing,182/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.hobie.com/articles/basics-sailing,182/</a><br /> <br /> 2. Nautical terms as explained via (of all things) Star Trek fandom. Slightly more disgestible than the straight wiki: <a href=\"https://memory-alpha.fandom.com/wiki/Nautical_terms\" target=\"_blank\">https://memory-alpha.fandom.com/wiki/Nautical_terms</a><br /> <br /> 3. Ship diagram for decks etc. Should just about serve for a blue-water vessel in Creation: <a href=\"https://imgur.com/YH5vslx\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/YH5vslx</a><br /> <br /> Would second Savage Seas if you can stretch to it though, it's got everything you should need.<br /> <br /> On Master &amp; Commander \u2013 my godfather, RN to his bones and snotty about anything to do with the sea in film/TV, nitpicked about one hammock knot and that was it. That's about as big an endorsement as I can give (I truly, truly love the books too, but they're not going to teach you sailing basics...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 12-17-2020, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T15:44:17-08:00","id":1428811,"title":"","content":"One of the things to be careful about in Creation, is that oar-powered vessels are still the default military ships. A Realm trained naval captain talking like they're from the Golden Age of Sail from Earth history is going to sound really weird (and give the wrong commands because they're going to be focused on oars in action scenes, not sails). This is primarily due to Exalted eschewing gunpowder based tech as cannons fairly radically changed naval warfare.<br /> <br /> This isn't a bad way to help differentiate the Western Threshold navies from the Realm's navies though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}